  "result": "I fixed two bugs in `src/`, and `npm test` now passes all 243 tests. I didn't change any test files.\n\n1. **Discount and tax were applied in the wrong order** (`src/cart.js`): `total()` added tax first and then took off the discount. The code's own comment says the discount comes off the pre-tax subtotal, so I swapped the order: discount first, then tax.\n2. **A fixed discount could make the total negative** (`src/discount.js`): a fixed discount larger than the amount gave a negative result, such as -14.5. It now stops at 0.\n\nThe tests were only failing on fixed discounts, but the first fix also changes results for percent discounts with tax.",
